= Relation — Simple =

A '''relation''' is a connection between things.

Examples:

* Alice '''is parent of''' Bob.
* A wheel '''is part of''' a bicycle.
* One program '''depends on''' another library.
* Five '''is greater than''' three.

Some relations have direction.

If A depends on B, that does not mean B depends on A.

Some relations are symmetric.

If A is a sibling of B, B is usually a sibling of A.

Some relations are transitive.

If A is greater than B and B is greater than C, A is greater than C.

But not every relation has these properties.

A [[Knowledge graph/Simple|knowledge graph]] often represents relations as labeled edges.

